{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q020_syntaxin_fragment_reclassification","answer":"In stable SCOPe 2.08, the fragments d1br0a_ and d1ez3a_/d1ez3b_/d1ez3c_, and full-domain structure d1dn1b_, are all assigned to the t-SNARE family a.47.2.1 (SUNID 47662), t-SNARE superfamily a.47.2 (SUNID 47661), STAT-like fold a.47 (SUNID 47654), and all-alpha class a. Thus the deepest common SCOPe level is family, supporting a close relationship among the classified syntaxin regions—not merely a generic three-helix resemblance. The fragments reside under the “Syntaxin 1A N-terminal domain” protein node (SUNID 47663); d1dn1b_ is instead recorded under “automated matches,” with the comment “automated match to d3c98b_,” so SCOPe directly supports their common family placement but not common protein-node membership.

The fragment caveat is essential: SCOPe describes d1br0a_ and every 1ez3 domain as a “three-helical fragment; similar to one spectrin repeat” and marks each ms, meaning secondary structures comprising less than one-third of the common domain are missing. The enclosing STAT-like fold is described as a four-long-helix bundle, whereas the separately classified Spectrin repeat-like fold is a.7 (SUNID 46965), described as a three-helix bundle. Consequently, resemblance of the truncated three-helix core to one spectrin repeat must not be promoted to a whole-domain spectrin-fold assignment, spectrin homology, or spectrin-like function. The complete-domain context supplied by 1dn1 B—and represented currently through its match to d3c98b_—changes the interpretation from “this fragment defines the fold” to “this fragment samples part of a larger t-SNARE/STAT-like domain.” SCOPe 1.75 already gives these entries the same a.47.2.1 placement, so the queried releases do not date an earlier reclassification or reveal its curator rationale.

For structural comparison or template use, 1br0 and 1ez3 should cover only their observed core: absent helices must not be scored as biological deletions, and the fragments are not interchangeable whole-domain templates. A complete-domain structure should anchor global topology and boundary decisions, but d1dn1 is obsolete in favor of 3c98, and no “best” representative can be selected without quality, coverage, conformational-state, and experimental-context evidence for every candidate. Likewise, family membership does not by itself transfer exact SNARE interactions, regulatory state, ligand/partner specificity, or biochemical function; resemblance to a spectrin repeat transfers none of spectrin’s mechanical or cytoskeletal roles. Establishing the detailed reason for the placement—or any relationship to spectrin beyond local shape—would require a complete-domain structural alignment, residue-level sequence correspondence across the full core, compatible domain context, and relevant phylogenetic or experimental/literature evidence. Different SCOPe folds mean that SCOPe makes no positive homology assertion between syntaxin and spectrin; they do not by themselves prove convergence or nonhomology.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","scop-homology/references/biological-interpretation.md","scop-homology/references/api-usage.md","mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info — /api/v1/; /api/v1/releases/current","mcp__scope__get_scop_pdb_entry — /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1br0; /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1br0/domains; /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1ez3; /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1ez3/domains; /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dn1; /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dn1/domains; /api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1br0/domains; /api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1ez3/domains; /api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1dn1/domains","mcp__scope__get_scop_domains — /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1br0a_; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1br0a_/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1br0a_/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3a_/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3a_/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3b_/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3c_/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dn1b_; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dn1b_/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dn1b_/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3c98b_; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3c98b_/parents","mcp__scope__search_scop — /api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=spectrin+repeat&mode=token&limit=20","mcp__scope__get_scop_node — /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/47654; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/47654/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/47654/homology; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/47661; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/47661/homology; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/47662; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/47662/homology; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/47663; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/46965; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/46965/parents; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/46965/annotations; /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/46965/homology"]}]}
